    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0101",
      "sequence": 956,
      "meaning": "Rāvaṇa raises a heretical illusion: fierce creatures, vetālas, ghosts and ghouls appear with bows and iron arrows; yoginīs wield swords and freshly severed human skulls, drink blood and dance. Crying ‘seize’ and ‘strike,’ open-mouthed apparitions pursue the monkeys, while fire blocks every path and sand rains down. Bears and monkeys collapse exhausted; Lakṣmaṇa, Sugrīva and all the heroes appear unconscious. Countless false Hanumāns then surround Rāma, snarling with raised tails. The dark Lord shines among them like a tall tamāla amid many rainbows. While the gods waver between joy and fear, Rāma destroys the illusion in the blink of an eye with one angry arrow. The restored monkeys seize trees and mountains; Rāma again shoots down Rāvaṇa’s arms and heads. Even Śeṣa, Sarasvatī, the Vedas and poets could not reach the end of the battle’s story through countless ages.",
