    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0102",
      "sequence": 957,
      "meaning": "The more Rāma cuts, the more Rāvaṇa’s heads multiply, as greed grows with every gain. Seeing the enemy will not die and that the Lord appears especially weary, Vibhīṣaṇa speaks. Śiva explains that the Lord whom Death itself kills only at his will is testing his servant’s love. Vibhīṣaṇa reveals that nectar resides in Rāvaṇa’s navel and sustains his life. The all-knowing Lord gladly takes a dreadful arrow. Evil omens erupt: jackals and dogs howl, birds utter cries of world-wide distress, comets appear, the quarters burn and an untimely eclipse covers the sun. Mandodarī’s heart trembles and images shed tears from their eyes.",
