    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0103",
      "sequence": 958,
      "meaning": "One arrow dries the nectar in Rāvaṇa’s navel while others sever his heads and arms and carry them away. The headless trunk dances and charges so violently that the earth sinks; Rāma splits it in two with another shaft. Dying, Rāvaṇa roars a challenge to Rāma. His fall shakes earth, sea, rivers, elephants of the quarters and mountains, and the two enormous halves crush crowds of bears and monkeys. The arrows lay his arms and heads before Mandodarī and return to the Lord’s quiver. Rāvaṇa’s radiance merges into Rāma’s face; Śiva, Brahmā, gods and sages rejoice, beat drums, fill the universe with cries of victory and shower flowers upon mighty-armed Raghubīra.",
