    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0104",
      "sequence": 959,
      "meaning": "Seeing her husband’s heads, Mandodarī faints and falls distraught to earth. The women lift her beside Rāvaṇa; with dishevelled hair and forgotten bodies they beat their breasts, cry out and recall his power. Earth once shook beneath his strength, fire, moon and sun lost brilliance, and neither Śeṣa nor the cosmic tortoise could bear his weight. Varuṇa, Kubera, Indra, Wind and even Death had not faced him steadily, yet now he lies like one abandoned. His fame, sons and family are gone and no one remains to mourn the line. Though the guardians of the quarters once bowed in fear, jackals now eat his heads and arms. Ruled by Time, he refused his wife’s counsel and mistook the Lord of all that moves and does not move for a mere man; such is the fitting end of one turned from Rāma.",
