    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0105",
      "sequence": 960,
      "meaning": "Hearing Mandodarī’s words, gods, sages and siddhas rejoice. Brahmā, Śiva, Nārada, Sanaka and the other seers of highest truth gaze upon Raghupati until their eyes are full and sink blissfully into love. Seeing the women lament, Vibhīṣaṇa approaches with a heavy heart and grieves at his brother’s state. Rāma sends Lakṣmaṇa to console him in many ways. The Lord then looks upon Vibhīṣaṇa graciously and commands him to put aside sorrow and perform the rites. Obeying, he conducts them properly according to place and time.",
