      "meaning": "The Lord calls Hanumān and sends him into Laṅkā to tell Jānakī the news and return with word of her welfare. Demons and demon-women hurry to honour the envoy and lead him to Sītā. Hanumān bows from a distance; recognizing Raghupati’s messenger, she asks after the gracious Lord, Lakṣmaṇa and the monkey army. He assures his mother that the Lord of Kosala and all his companions are well, that Rāma has conquered and killed the ten-headed enemy, and that Vibhīṣaṇa has received an unshakable kingdom. Joy fills Sītā’s heart.",
