      "sequence": 964,
      "meaning": "Accepting the Lord’s words, Sītā—pure in mind, deed and speech—asks Lakṣmaṇa to act as minister of the sacred rite and quickly kindle a fire. Her speech, steeped in separation, discernment, dharma and principle, fills his eyes with tears; with folded hands he cannot answer the Lord. Reading Rāma’s expression, he brings wood and lights a strong blaze. Vaidehī sees it without fear and with joy, declaring that if her heart has no refuge other than Raghubīra in thought, word or deed, then Fire, knower of every creature’s course, should become cool as sandalwood for her.",
