      "sequence": 965,
      "meaning": "The pinned text resumes with Mātali receiving Raghupati’s permission, bowing at his feet and departing. The habitually self-interested gods arrive and speak as though devoted to the highest good: they praise compassionate Rāma for rescuing them, condemn the lustful, world-hating Rāvaṇa who met the evil course earned by his sins, and acclaim the Lord as imperishable Brahman—unchanging, desireless, unborn, sinless, invincible and unfailingly powerful. Recalling his fish, tortoise, boar, man-lion, dwarf and Paraśurāma forms, they say he assumes many bodies whenever the gods suffer. They marvel that the worst offender reached his feet, confess that although privileged gods they forgot devotion through self-interest and remain swept along becoming, and seek his protection.",
